{"book":23,"chapter":49,"context":{"chapter":49,"title":"A Light to the Gentiles","summary":"The Servant, called from the womb, feels he has labored in vain, but God gives him a larger task: to be a light to the Gentiles. When Zion says God has forgotten her, He answers that a mother may forget her nursing child, but He will never forget Zion.","background":"This second Servant Song (vv. 1–13) calls the servant 'Israel' (v. 3) yet gives him a mission to Israel (vv. 5–6), so many readers see an individual who embodies the nation. Paul and Barnabas quote verse 6 to explain their mission to the Gentiles (Acts 13:47).","customs":[{"term":"Graven upon the palms","verses":"49:16","note":"People sometimes wrote a name on the hand as a sign of belonging (compare 44:5). God has engraved Zion on His own hands."}],"watchFor":["'I have laboured in vain' (v. 4) is met by a bigger calling (v. 6).","The mother who cannot forget her child (v. 15).","Zion, who thought she was childless, finds her home too small (vv. 19–21)."],"connections":["Acts 13:47","2 Corinthians 6:2","Luke 2:32","Revelation 7:16-17"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["שִׁמְעוּ","shim'u","H8085","HVqv2mp","listen"],["אִיִּים","'iyim","H339","HNcmpa","O islands"],["אֵלַי","'elai","H413","HR/Sp1bs","to me"],["וְהַקְשִׁיבוּ","vehakshivu","H7181","HC/Vhv2mp","and pay attention"],["לְאֻמִּים","le'umim","H3816","HNcmpa","O peoples"],["מֵרָחוֹק","merachok","H7350","HR/Aamsa","from a distance"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["מִבֶּטֶן","mibeten","H990","HR/Ncfsa","from [the] womb"],["קְרָאָנִי","kera'ani","H7121","HVqp3ms/Sp1bs","he called me"],["מִמְּעֵי","mime'ei","H4578","HR/Ncmpc","from [the] inward parts of"],["אִמִּי","'imi","H517","HNcfsc/Sp1bs","mother my"],["הִזְכִּיר","hizkir","H2142","HVhp3ms","he has brought to remembrance"],["שְׁמִי","shemi","H8034","HNcmsc/Sp1bs","name my"]],"x":[[24001005,24001005,18],[48001015,48001015,14],[23044002,23044002,10],[23049005,23049005,9],[42001031,42001031,8],[19071005,19